\details{
The season's competition is picked from the \code{NZNBL} chooser by the label rule include = \verb{national basketball league|sals nbl}, exclude = \code{rapid|women} (case-insensitive); cups and play-offs have their own \code{comp_id}. Several matching competitions raise \code{hoopR_bad_request} (pass \code{comp_id}); none raises \code{hoopR_no_data}.

Genius match ids are one global sequence shared by every customer and \code{data.json} names no competition, so each game alias checks the id on the game's LiveStats shell (\verb{/u/NZN/<match_id>/}: one extra request per game, cached per process for an hour): its competition name must pass the label rule. Another org's game, a cup or play-off game of \code{NZNBL}, or a shell request that fails twice (or names no competition) raises \code{hoopR_asset_fetch}. The base \verb{genius_*()} function reads any game unchecked.

